        "content": "RAPID RESPONSE activated for acute hypotension unresponsive to 1L fluid resuscitation. Current vitals: BP 78/40, HR 122, RR 24, SpO2 92% on 4L NC, T 38.0\u00c2\u00b0C. Patient alert but distressed. Second large-bore IV placed. Rapid response team at bedside. Labs redrawn STAT including type and screen, coags, lactate."
      },
      {
        "type": "Discharge Summary",
        "author": "Dr. James Park, Hematology",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-20T00:00:00",
        "title": "Discharge Summary \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (2023)",
        "content": "ADMISSION DATE: 2023-10-28\nDISCHARGE DATE: 2023-11-20\nATTENDING: Dr. James Park, Hematology\n\nDIAGNOSES:\n1. Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (HIT) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d confirmed\n2. Left lower extremity deep vein thrombosis\n3. Hypertension\n4. Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS:\nMr. Chen is a 64-year-old male admitted on 10/28/2023 for left calf swelling and pain. Ultrasound confirmed acute DVT of the left popliteal and femoral veins. Started on unfractionated heparin drip. On hospital day 7, platelet count dropped from 198 to 68 (66% decline). 4Ts score calculated at 7 (high probability). Heparin was immediately discontinued. PF4/heparin antibody ELISA strongly positive (OD 2.4). Serotonin release assay confirmed positive. Transitioned to argatroban with subsequent platelet recovery.\n\n4Ts SCORE CALCULATION (2023):\n- Thrombocytopenia: >50% fall, nadir \u00e2\u2030\u00a520 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d 2 points\n- Timing: Day 7 of heparin exposure \u00e2\u20ac\u201d 2 points\n- Thrombosis: Confirmed DVT \u00e2\u20ac\u201d 2 points\n- Other causes: None evident \u00e2\u20ac\u201d 1 point\n- TOTAL: 7/8 (High probability)\n\nHOSPITAL COURSE:\nArgatroban initiated at 2 mcg/kg/min, titrated to aPTT 1.5-3x baseline. Platelets recovered to 156 by day 10 of argatroban. Transitioned to warfarin with INR overlap. Duplex at discharge showed improving DVT. Patient counseled extensively about lifelong heparin avoidance including low-molecular-weight heparins, heparin flushes, and heparin-coated devices.\n\nCRITICAL ALLERGY UPDATE:\n*** HEPARIN \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ALL FORMS \u00e2\u20ac\u201d CONTRAINDICATED ***\nIncluding: unfractionated heparin, enoxaparin, dalteparin, heparin flushes, heparin-bonded catheters.\nAlternative anticoagulants: argatroban, bivalirudin, fondaparinux (with caution).\n\nDISCHARGE MEDICATIONS:\n- Warfarin 5mg daily (target INR 2-3)\n- Lisinopril 20mg daily\n- Metformin 1000mg BID\n- Atorvastatin 40mg daily\n\nFOLLOW-UP: Hematology clinic 2 weeks. PCP 1 week. INR check in 3 days.\n\nSIGNED: Dr. James Park, MD, Hematology\nDate: 2023-11-20"
      }
    ],
